<title>POLAND: POLL - POLISH BANKS TO UP CREDIT, DEPOSIT RATES.</title>
<headline>POLL - POLISH BANKS TO UP CREDIT, DEPOSIT RATES.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish commercial banks are expected to increase their credit and deposit rates in August and hold them relatively flat until the end of the year, a monthly poll by daily Dziennik Prawa i Gospodarki said.</p>
<p>The rate increases follow the National Bank of Poland's decision to increase its official interest rates by two and 2.5 points to 27 and 24.5 percent on August 4.</p>
<p>				    NOW  END-AUGUST  END-1997  JULY 98</p>
<p> Call deposits (in pct)     8.9     8.9	  9.0	 8.6</p>
<p> 3-month depos		 17.5    17.7	 17.7	16.6</p>
<p> 6-month depos		 18.5    18.7	 18.7	17.6</p>
<p> 12-month depos		19.5    19.7	 19.8	18.6</p>
<p> Credit for firms	    24.5    25.2	 25.2	24.0</p>
<p> 12-m consumption credit   26.5    27.2	 27.2	25.7</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
